 problem="A missed call is rarely a customer who calls back. They call the next name on the list. Most small companies know this and still miss a third of their calls, because the person who could answer is holding a drill, a client, or a child. The usual fix is an answering service that reads a script and takes a message — which is a slower way of not answering.",
